nd Norvane Utilities by 12%. Most of that is substations and transformers. Pellham is the largest single buyer of grid equipment in Caldria (doc `utility-capex-2027`).\n- **Data centres:** Grid connection requests are expected to grow 9% in 2027. That is slower than in 2026, because power availability limits new sites (doc `datacentre-demand`).\n- **Exposure of VLTX holdings:** Utilities are 62% of its orders. Pellham is 35% of those utility orders and Norvane is 21%, so the two together are 56% of utility orders (doc `vltx-order-mix`). That makes VLTX holdings' demand outlook depend heavily on Pellham's plans.\n\n**Caveats:**\n- The utility figures are plans, not orders. Whether Pellham and Norvane can finance them is being assessed separately by n3. One data point there: utility bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 2026 to 165bp, and equity markets have been less receptive (doc `utility-credit`).\n- Because the data-centre growth rate is falling, utilities are the main driver of demand.","ttft_ms":2777,"type":"result","duration_ms":18028,"uuid":"344b7884-0f11-4962-b6df-42e12025bdce","ttft_stream_ms":2178,"time_to_request_ms":381,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":26,"system_prompt":35,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":17,"input_attachments":78,"input_hooks":17,"conversation_append":16,"transcript_persist":10,"tool_pool_refresh":7,"init_message":28,"init_frame_send":6,"engine_pickup":3,"loop_entry":11,"message_prep":8,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":14,"request_announcements":51,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":4,"tool_schema_build":13,"message_normalization":10,"client_creation":9,"request_build":16},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":163,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":75,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":171,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":96,"process_rss_mib_result":189,"process_anon_mib_result":108,"process_peak_rss_mib":189,"process_cpu_ms_turn":515,"process_wall_ms_turn":18027,"process_cp